deckcraft — self-built HTML-first presentation skill for Ultrawork.

Portions of this skill are adapted from ppt-master (https://github.com/hugohe3/ppt-master),
Copyright (c) 2025-2026 Hugo He, MIT License (see LICENSE-ppt-master):
  - scripts/source_to_md/  (document → Markdown converters)
    Local modifications: doc_to_md.py adds CREATE_NO_WINDOW to the pandoc
    subprocess (ADR-054 convention); web_to_md.py docstring no longer points
    at the un-shipped Node.js fallback script.
  - scripts/console_encoding.py (unmodified)
  - assets/icons/tabler-outline/  (Tabler Icons, MIT, https://tabler.io/icons —
    copied via ppt-master's icon library, unmodified)

The editable-pptx export (P2b, --pptx-editable) bundles:
  - scripts/html2pptx/vendor/pptxgen.vendor.cjs — pptxgenjs
    (https://github.com/gitbrent/PptxGenJS), Copyright (c) 2015-2023 Brent Ely,
    MIT License, with its jszip dependency (MIT) inlined via esbuild. This is a
    redistributed build; regeneration is documented in that dir's README.md.

Design-system methodology draws on published MIT-licensed projects
(frontend-slides, huashu-design) — ideas only, no code copied. The
html2pptx element-translation approach (getComputedStyle + getBoundingClientRect
per element → pptxgenjs primitives) is informed by huashu-design's method; no
code was copied.
